  "date": "2026-08-06T18:56:51Z",
  "subject": "refactor: kind harness mirrors the tenant topology; platform-owned components are kind-only",
  "body": "Plan 5 Task 4. Retires the divergent kind rig in favor of a real mirror\nof the tenant topology: three Applications (datalake-storage/compute/\norchestration, environments/kind/apps/) pointing at the same\nenvs/prod/<tier> charts prod uses, differing only by values-kind.yaml.\n\n- Moved the five platform-owned operator Applications (CloudNativePG,\n  External Secrets, Argo Workflows, Dex, kube-prometheus-stack) + MinIO\n  from apps/infra/ into environments/kind/infra/ -- kind-only now, prod\n  gets them from the platform. Bumped each to newest stable (matching the\n  plan's Context line: CNPG 0.29.0/1.30, External Secrets 2.8.0, Argo\n  Workflows 1.0.23/v4.0.8, kube-prometheus-stack 88.1.5) and fixed\n  controller.workflowNamespaces (chart default [\"default\"] would have\n  silently never run our CronWorkflows in datalake-orchestration).\n- Added a kind-only `platform` ClusterSecretStore (ESO Kubernetes\n  provider, remoteNamespace eso-secret-source) -- same name as\n  production, so every ExternalSecret the tier charts render is\n  byte-identical across environments.\n- Populated the three values-kind.yaml placeholders: node placement\n  (labels the kind worker pool=db -- storage tier's real nodeSelector\n  exercises for real; compute's cpu=x86-64-v3 stays neutralised, not\n  labelled -- this host's CPU lacks AVX2, verified live, and the\n  committed Trino 480 pin SIGILLs here, so kind pins back to the\n  historical 476 digest instead), local-path storage class, restored\n  historical kind overrides (helloCron/echoReceiver enabled, landing-db\n  sizing, tightened nightly schedule -- sitesonar deliberately NOT\n  tightened, see that file's comment: Task 3's ExternalSecret can no\n  longer thread SITESONAR_LIMIT through, and this host has ~20Gi free).\n- Relaxed the SHOW CATALOGS gate from an exact set to an allowlist\n  ({lake, landing, system, tpch, tpcds}) plus a required {lake, landing}\n  pair -- Helm's dependency-values null-propagation only deletes the\n  trino subchart's default tpch/tpcds catalogs once a second values file\n  also touches `trino:` (confirmed empirically), so the rendered set\n  differs between kind and a bare prod render; the gate now passes either\n  way instead of assuming one.\n- Added a live CNPG `job`-label verification gate (queries Prometheus for\n  cnpg_pg_replication_streaming_replicas once both database clusters are\n  up) -- the storage tier's alert exprs assume job=\"<namespace>/<cluster>\";\n  confirmed live, load-bearing on the PodMonitor being named after the\n  CNPG cluster, not a CNPG-exporter guarantee as the alert file's own\n  comment implies.\n- Rewired hack/*.sh off the deleted chart/ path and the old per-component\n  namespaces (lakekeeper/landing-db/trino/argo-workflows) onto the three\n  tenant namespaces; kind-up.sh now provisions ESO-backed remote secrets\n  in eso-secret-source instead of writing target Secrets directly.\n- Deleted environments/cyfronet/ (its ArgoCD-hydrator-against-cyfronet\n  model is superseded by the platform's own hub ArgoCD -- Task 5 defines\n  the real prod entry point) and apps/ (nothing under it applied to prod\n  any more; environments/kind/project.yaml replaces apps/project.yaml).\n\nmake lint green (3 tier charts x prod+kind values, seam gate, Application/\nAppProject kubeconform).\n\n(per Task 4 in deliverables/plans/2026-08-06-datalake-v2-tenant-port-plan.md)\n"
}
